% Axiom contradictions for kernel: fiat_efficacy_kernel
% Source: SCOPE axiom_contradictions declaration (independent of edge types).
% contradiction + coexists_with edge = licensed plurality
% contradiction + forecloses edge    = real closure

:- multifile narrative_ontology:cs_axiom_contradiction/2.

% truth_procedure_reading↔utopian_fiction_reading: The truth-procedure reading holds that fiat constitutes a real ontological event that transforms subjects and forces the State to change (efficacy is metaphysically real and binding on the world); the utopian-fiction reading holds that fiat is explicitly and only a game/fiction whose value is pedagogical, with no claim to force actual state change. A framework cannot simultaneously hold that fiat is a world-transforming truth-event AND that it is merely an educational game bracketed from the real political field — accepting one axiom requires rejecting the metaphysical seriousness (or unseriousness) claimed by the other.
% empirical_precedent_reading↔empathy_simulation_reading: The empirical-precedent reading locates efficacy in external, material, measurable outcomes (troop withdrawal, national policy attention) as the criterion of success; the empathy-simulation reading explicitly locates efficacy in internal psychological/attitudinal change independent of and prior to any external policy outcome. A framework holding that only external material outcomes count as evidence of efficacy cannot simultaneously hold that purely internal attitude change is sufficient efficacy on its own terms — one must subordinate the other.

narrative_ontology:cs_axiom_contradiction(efficacy_located_in_subjective_ontological_break, value_located_in_practice_not_formal_power).
narrative_ontology:cs_axiom_contradiction(value_located_in_practice_not_formal_power, efficacy_located_in_subjective_ontological_break).
